<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan M-2 rises 2.83 percent in week to Dec 6.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan M-2 rises 2.83 percent in week to Dec 6.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan money supply, as measured by the monetary aggregate M-2, rose 2.83 percent or 140 billion bolivars to 5.081 trillion bolivars in the week to Dec 6, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1996, M-2 was 3.530 trillion bolivars.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
